Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Doll City project.

## What was implemented:

1. **Installed @vercel/analytics package**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` as a dependency in package.json
   - Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency and its 5 sub-dependencies

2. **Configured Analytics for Static HTML Site**
   - Added Vercel Analytics script tag to `index.html` in the head section
   - Used the CDN-hosted script approach: `<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>`
   - Script placement: After font stylesheet links, before the style tag

3. **Build Verification**
   - Ran `npm run build` successfully - build completed without errors
   - Verified that the analytics script is included in the built output (dist/index.html and dist/embed.html)
   - Build size: 888 KB (same as before, script loads asynchronously from CDN)

## Files Modified:

- `/index.html` - Added Vercel Analytics script tag
- `/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `/dist/index.html` - Built output including analytics script
- `/dist/embed.html` - Built embed version including analytics script
- `/dist/sw.js` - Updated service worker with new version hash

## Implementation Details:

This is a static HTML/JavaScript game built with esbuild. Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation, I used the recommended approach for HTML/static sites:
- Script is loaded from Vercel's CDN (https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js)
- Uses `defer` attribute for optimal performance (loads asynchronously, executes after DOM parsing)
- No additional configuration needed - analytics will automatically track page views
- Script is included in the source HTML and gets bundled into the final build

The analytics will be active once the site is deployed to Vercel. The script automatically handles:
- Page view tracking
- Web Vitals metrics (CLS, FID, LCP, FCP, TTFB)
- Cross-domain tracking if configured in Vercel dashboard

## Testing:

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ Analytics script verified in build output
✅ No linting errors (project has no lint scripts configured)
✅ No test failures (project has no test scripts configured)

## Next Steps:

To activate analytics:
1. Deploy to Vercel or push to your connected repository
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)
3. Analytics data will start appearing within 24 hours of deployment
